      "notes": "60 degrees of hip flexion, which is what lengthens the hamstrings (they run pelvis->tibia). The rig is pelvis-rooted, so the body pivots about the hips rather than keeping the heels planted -- holding a ground contact through this range needs a real IK solve, not a joint-angle clip. Counter-rotating Hips to fake it does not work: Hips is the rig root and carries the spine, arms and head with it, which visibly tore the body apart.",
